{
  "reason": "Child lifecycle rows belong to their owning process. Adjacent notices form a bounded group with the latest notice per child; completion folds that process rather than deleting records or leaving a terminal tail. Saved late notices remain in the original process across later turns. A receipt whose named turn is absent from the transcript has no owner to settle into and is dropped instead of stranding at the tail.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "completed child releases earlier start",
      "events": [
